# roles/ is deliberately NOT listed here.
#
# That does not mean role requests merge themselves — branch protection still
# requires a human approval, and nothing in this repository has a ruleset
# bypass. It means the approver does not have to be the platform team. A file
# in roles/ can only select bundles from the catalogue, and every role it
# produces is capped by a permissions boundary this repository cannot change,
# so approving one is a judgement about whether the application should exist,
# not an IAM review. Anyone on the platform team can give it in seconds, with
# the plan comment in front of them.
#
# Everything below can widen what a vended role may do, so it needs the people
# who own that decision.

# Raw IAM statements. The escape hatch exists because the catalogue will never
# cover everything; it is a separate directory rather than a field inside the
# requesting team's own file precisely so that this line can gate it.
/exceptions/ @bernadin-kabore

# main.tf holds the pinned module ref. Moving that pin changes what
# self-service is able to ask for, for every role vended here.
/main.tf @bernadin-kabore
/providers.tf @bernadin-kabore
/backend.tf @bernadin-kabore
/variables.tf @bernadin-kabore

# The pipeline that holds the credential able to create IAM roles.
/.github/ @bernadin-kabore
